message: "If you use the TensorCube 11D Order-4 experiment in research, please cite this software artifact."
title: "TensorCube 11D Order-4: GPU Tensor Iteration Solver"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Wong"
    given-names: "Zining Kestis"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MatrixFreeSama/TensorCube/tree/11d-order4"
url: "https://github.com/MatrixFreeSama/TensorCube/tree/11d-order4"
date-released: 2026-08-12
license-url: "https://github.com/MatrixFreeSama/TensorCube/blob/11d-order4/LICENSE"
abstract: >-
  TensorCube 11D Order-4 is an eleven-dimensional order-4 discrete rotation
  experiment using an explicit authoritative i/s/R StateVector with Matrix-Free
  sparse legal operators. The solver derives the legal parity quotient and
  sparse source-macro factorization from the current state, verifies all
  4,192,256 surface identities and complete signed 11-axis orientations, and
  does not consume random-generation secrets or retained scramble history.
keywords:
  - matrix-free
  - state-only factorization
  - eleven-dimensional
  - exact verification
  - discrete reconfiguration
  - scientific computing
  - tensor iteration
